WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.389
Film Courage: When did you start calling yourself
a screenwriter?

00:00:03.389 --> 00:00:06.540
Travis Seppala, Author/Screenwriter: Probably
my second or third script?

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:10.401
Like my first script was kind of I was writing
about like a personal experience and I was

00:00:10.401 --> 00:00:15.550
just kind of it was almost like therapy for
me at the time and so then probably my second

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:18.610
script I was an “aspiring” screenwriter.

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:19.680
I was like Oh this is fun!

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:20.680
I want to do this.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.573
And probably I got to me third maybe fourth
script was when I was like Oh yeah, I’m

00:00:23.573 --> 00:00:24.573
a screenwriter.

00:00:24.573 --> 00:00:27.210
I’m not getting paid yet but I’m a screenwriter,
like this is where I’m going.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:31.690
And then my fifth script was a paid script
so I was like I already made it come true,

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:32.690
awesome!

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:36.039
It was very big pay because it was a small
local person.

00:00:36.039 --> 00:00:40.850
I think I got like $500 bucks our something
to write a feature.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:41.850
That never got made.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:46.429
But yes probably by my third or fourth script
is when I went from being an aspiring screenwriter

00:00:46.429 --> 00:00:48.850
to yes this is what I’m doing with my life.

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:52.819
Film Courage: Did someone say to you don’t
call yourself an “aspiring” writer?

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:56.900
Travis: Oh you will always get haters who
say like if you’re not making money at it

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.159
you shouldn’t call yourself a screenwriter.

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:03.589
They are like Oh you wouldn’t call yourself
a plumber because you fixed your own toilet.

00:01:03.589 --> 00:01:09.380
Well I’m still writing screenplays and I’m
not doing it just for myself, I’m still

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:12.549
trying to get myself out into the world whether
it’s being paid or not because you know

00:01:12.549 --> 00:01:16.310
when you’re writing a spec script you’re
not paid through writing that spec.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:18.850
So are you not a screenwriter because it hasn’t
sold?

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:20.090
You still wrote the thing.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:23.729
It takes time, effort, energy, heart, blood,
soul.

00:01:23.729 --> 00:01:25.390
Everything goes into these scripts.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:29.539
So you’re absolutely, if you’re actually
doing the work, you’re absolutely a screenwriter.

00:01:29.539 --> 00:01:35.290
I feel like the only way that you’re not
is if you’re someone who says you’re a

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.359
screenwriter and aren’t doing any work towards
it.

00:01:37.359 --> 00:01:40.200
I’ve met people who are like “I’m a
screenwriter.”

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.360
“Okay, great.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:42.360
What have you worked on?”

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.850
“Oh well…I haven’t written anything
yet but I want to be.”

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.280
Film Courage: Welcome to Los Angeles.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:47.280
Travis: Exactly.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.280
There you go.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:55.210
I heard on Twitter…I follow a lot of show
runners and stuff like that and there was

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.590
a show runner I’m trying to remember who
it was now.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:03.270
It was a couple of weeks ago that they met
someone at a party, they knew who she was,

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:07.990
and what show she was on and they were like
“Oh well I would love to write on your show,

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:08.990
that’s fantastic.”

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:13.530
And they had built a rapport before we brought
it up which is good and she was “Okay, be

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:15.140
sure to send me over a sample.”

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:16.420
He didn’t have any samples!

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:20.110
He had not written a single thing but he’s
telling her how much he wants to write for

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:27.310
her show and it’s like why are you bringing
that up if you don’t have anything to show

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:34.660
and prove yourself to them because like Oh
well in that case I want to go and play baseball

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:37.410
but I don’t have the experience on it I
want to.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:40.830
So as soon as you’re doing the work, you’re
a screenwriter.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:45.350
Film Courage: Okay, that makes sense and so
what I was also wondering is did you feel

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:49.820
like you held yourself back because you were
calling yourself (I think after your second

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:51.870
script) an aspiring writer?

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.880
Travis: I don’t think I was holding myself
back.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:59.730
I think it was like I didn’t have the nerve
to call myself that yet because I was so inexperienced

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:04.880
and I wasn’t sure if that’s what I wanted
to so and be with and have as my career.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:09.710
It was something at the time fun because like
I said the first script I wrote is like therapy

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.750
for a situation I was in at the time.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:16.540
My second script I wrote a Superman script
not knowing you can’t write material because

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:20.670
of copyright infringements and stuff like
that but I didn’t know it was a thing yet

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:21.670
at the time.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:26.380
I was in my like early twenties so I didn’t
really know that you couldn’t write a Superman

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:31.820
script and send it out there but it was fun
and figured out what does and doesn’t work

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:35.230
in the writing especially for action sequences.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:39.560
But then by my third and fourth thing like
I said I was starting to write my own original

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:43.830
material at that point then and that’s when
I became a screenwriter as opposed to just

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:44.972
somebody who has fun doing it.

00:03:44.972 --> 00:03:44.989
Question For The Viewers: When can you call
yourself a screenwriter?

